Wrote `/app/answer.sql`: a CTE aggregates Q4 2024 revenue per product (`SUM(quantity * unit_price)`, half-open `[2024-10-01, 2025-01-01)` on `order_date`), then `RANK() OVER (PARTITION BY category ORDER BY sales DESC)` keeps `rnk <= 3`.

Check: ran the exact pipeline snippet from the task (duckdb 1.3.2 / pandas 2.1.4 in `.venv`) and compared against an independent pandas groupby — both produce the same 15 rows, 3 per category across all 5 categories (`Clothing`, `Electronics`, `Grocery`, `Home`, `Toys`). Output columns are `category, product_id, sales`, so the `.groupby('category')['product_id'].apply(list).to_dict()` extraction works as written.

Two choices worth flagging: "sales" is read as revenue, not unit count, and `RANK()` (rather than `ROW_NUMBER()`) keeps ties at the boundary — I checked there are none in this data, so both would agree here.

